  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1026 PM CDT Thu Jul 23 2026\n\nAfter some lingering precip Saturday morning, subtle height rises\nunfold during the day as the upper high nudges east and atop \nsouthern Colorado by the evening. This presents us with more \nsubsidence, yet we'll retain low chances for additional afternoon \nstorms underneath a lingering band of mid-level moisture. This \nelevated moist layer dries out on Sunday as the upper ridge \nbroadens, but high temps should only nudge a few degrees higher \nthan Saturday thanks to southeast flow at H7 that keeps a harsh \nthermal ridge to our north where places like eastern Colorado and\nwestern Kansas could see highs touch 110. As the upper high wobbles\nsouth toward the Texas Panhandle on Monday and decays from 600 \ndam to 596 dam, our temps will slowly climb with Heat Advisories \na good bet for areas off the Caprock through at least midweek. \nModels agree in the high retreating into New Mexico by Wednesday \nwhich sadly is still too close to offer us any reprieve from the \ntriple-digit heat.",
